# Email Simulation Engine (ESE)

ESE is the email simulation component I'm building as part of PX-C5.

The goal is to build it step by step while actually understanding how each part works, rather than relying on code I don't understand.

# Current Focus

I'm currently building the foundation of the engine, starting with:

Python fundamentals
SMTP connections
Connecting to an SMTP server
TLS with starttls()
SMTP authentication with login()
Closing SMTP sessions
Building the basic CampaignEngine structure

# Planned Development

As the engine develops, it will eventually cover more of the email simulation workflow.

For now, I'm deliberately keeping the scope small and focusing on understanding and building each part before moving on.

# Documentation

The development and learning process is documented through individual notes and milestones.

Daily Winter Arc logs → ../../logs/
ESE technical notes and milestones → this directory
Principle

Understand it first. Build it second.

I want to be able to explain, debug, modify, and extend the engine independently rather than just having working code.
